{# DEF-111 — Ordnance Survey grid reference input.

   Delegates entirely to govukInput. There is no forked markup here: the value
   of the component is that the format, the hint, the width and the input
   attributes are decided once instead of by every team that needs one.

   Decisions worth keeping:

   - autocapitalize="characters". The two-letter prefix is always upper case
     and phone keyboards default to lower.
   - No `pattern` by default. A pattern that rejects a valid reference is worse
     than none, references vary in precision (SU 12 34 through SU 1234 5678),
     and the server has to validate regardless. Callers can still pass one.
   - width-10, which fits the longest common form without implying more
     precision than is being asked for.
   - spellcheck off — a grid reference is not a word. #}
{% from "govuk/components/input/macro.njk" import govukInput %}

{{ govukInput({
  id: params.id | default("grid-reference"),
  name: params.name | default("gridReference"),
  value: params.value,
  classes: ("govuk-input--width-10 " + params.classes) if params.classes else "govuk-input--width-10",
  label: params.label | default({ text: "Grid reference" }),
  hint: params.hint | default({ text: "For example, SU 1234 5678" }),
  errorMessage: params.errorMessage,
  autocomplete: "off",
  spellcheck: false,
  autocapitalize: "characters",
  attributes: params.attributes
}) }}
